# The CONTACT_MATRIX between GROUPA (5 atoms) and GROUPB (95 atoms) is non-square and,
# with D_MAX, it is stored as a sparse matrix. Forces reach it element by element through
# FLATTEN. forces.reference was generated with the equivalent input that does not use
# FLATTEN (biases on the matrix directly), so the two routes must give the same forces.
arg="--plumed plumed.dat --ixyz traj.xyz --length-units 1 --dump-forces forces --dump-forces-fmt=%10.5f"
